      "writtenOn": "2022-10-11T13:48:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, the idea of control flow being uniform or not is different from the control flow restrictions that ES2 imposes. You can still have non-uniform control flow, it\u0027s really just that the rules are written to allow devices with no real branching support. Any device that has real branching could still end up with problems.\n\nEven without branching, a typical minimum-spec ES2 device like skvm will elide writes to locals when lanes are dead, which can cause the derivative instructions to produce nonsense or uninitialized data:\n\n    vec2 uv;\n    vec4 color;\n    if (someCondition) {\n      uv \u003d pos * scale;  // This won\u0027t happen for pixels with !someCondition\n      color \u003d texture2D(texA, uv);  // Oops, gradients are going to be busted\n    } else {\n      uv \u003d pos + offset;\n      color \u003d texture2D(texB, uv);\n    }\n    // More code that uses uv, perhaps?",
      "parentUuid": "cc497487_5e896cf0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 95,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 95,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "3a62357ae025ba831ff20b8c759537ca7eb744ff",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
